{"path":"io/basic_ios/clear","title":"std::basic_ios<CharT,Traits>::clear","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_ios&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>clear","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/clear","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Sets the stream error state flags by assigning them the value of state. By default, assigns std::ios_base::goodbit which has the effect of clearing all error state flags.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><span class=\"kw1714\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">iostate</span></span></a> state <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><span class=\"kw1715\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">goodbit</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Sets the stream error state flags by assigning them the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">state</span></code>. By default, assigns <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\">std::ios_base::goodbit</a></span> which has the effect of clearing all error state flags.\n</p><p>If <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/rdbuf\">rdbuf()</a></span> is a null pointer (i.e. there is no associated stream buffer), then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">state <span class=\"sy3\">|</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><span class=\"kw1716\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">badbit</span></span></a></span></code> is assigned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> state\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> new error state flags setting. It can be a combination of the following constants:\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Constant\n</td>\n<td> Explanation\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><code>goodbit</code></a>\n</td>\n<td> no error\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><code>badbit</code></a>\n</td>\n<td> irrecoverable stream error\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><code>failbit</code></a>\n</td>\n<td> input/output operation failed (formatting or extraction error)\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><code>eofbit</code></a>\n</td>\n<td> associated input sequence has reached end-of-file\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>If the new error state includes a bit that is also included in the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/exceptions\">exceptions()</a></span> mask, throws an exception of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\">failure</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p><code>clear()</code> without arguments can be used to unset the <a href=\"#Parameters\"><code>failbit</code></a> after unexpected input; for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cin\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cin</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">putback</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>c<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> see <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/ungetc#Notes\"><code>ungetc</code></a>.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'4'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'1'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'.'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'3'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'Z'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'Y'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'X'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cin\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cin</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">putback</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// emulate user's input (not portable: see ungetc Notes)</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Please, enter a number: \"</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cin\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cin</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> n<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cin\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cin</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">clear</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> line<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/getline\"><span class=\"kw1264\">std::<span class=\"me2\">getline</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cin\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cin</span></span></a>, line<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> line <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>I am sorry, but '\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> line <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"' is not a number<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>Thank you for entering the number \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Please, enter a number: XYZ\nI am sorry, but 'XYZ' is not a number\nPlease, enter a number: 3.14\nThank you for entering the number 3.14</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue412\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 412</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>an excption would be thrown if the current error state<br>includes a bit that is also included in the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/exceptions\">exceptions()</a></span> mask\n</td>\n<td>checks the new<br>error state instead\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/setstate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>setstate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  sets state flags <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/rdstate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>rdstate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns state flags <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_ios","title":"std::basic_ios"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_ios<CharT,Traits>::clear","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Sets the stream error state flags by assigning them the value of state."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"state","children":[{"label":"goodbit","note":"no error"},{"label":"badbit","note":"irrecoverable stream error"},{"label":"failbit","note":"input/output operation failed (formatting or extraction error)"},{"label":"eofbit","note":"associated input sequence has reached end-of-file"}]},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"If the new error state includes a bit that is also included in the exceptions() mask, throws an exception of type failure."},{"label":"Example","note":"clear() without arguments can be used to unset the failbit after unexpected input; for std::cin.putback(c) see ungetc."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"setstate","note":"sets state flags"},{"label":"rdstate","note":"returns state flags"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":316,"codeBlockCount":2}
